                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Internal medicine, a specialty within clinical medicine, encompasses specialties including Respiratory and Critical Care, Cardiology, Gastroenterology, Nephrology, Hematology, Endocrinology & Metabolism, Rheumatology, Infectious Diseases, Oncology, and Geriatrics. Its core covers disease definition, etiology, pathogenesis, epidemiology, symptoms, signs, lab/auxiliary exams, diagnosis/differential diagnosis, treatment, and prognosis. The curriculum strengthens humanistic medical education and medical ethics, promoting the physician spirit of "truth, goodness, beauty." It aims to cultivate innovative outstanding medical talents who uphold original aspirations, forge convictions, strengthen humanism, and embrace great love—to serve patients better and lay foundations for disciplinary development.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
